        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Northrop F-15 Reporter, RF-61, Northrop P-61 Black Widow\n- Companies: Northrop\n- Concepts: photographic reconnaissance aircraft, night fighter, radar\n\nFacts:\n- The Northrop P-61 Black Widow was named for the American spider.\n- The Northrop P-61 Black Widow was the first operational U.S. warplane designed as a night fighter.\n- The Northrop P-61 Black Widow was the first aircraft designed to use radar.\n- The Northrop F-15 Reporter was an American unarmed photographic reconnaissance aircraft.\n- The Northrop F-15 Reporter was later redesignated RF-61.",
